    {
      "id": "claim_16745439639644a39ac87c5711149f50",
      "statement": "IJob has exactly two members with queue semantics: Key is the admission token used for deduplication rather than an identifier the queue logs or persists, and RunAsync receives a per-job AsyncServiceScope's IServiceProvider plus the shutdown token; the queue names no concrete job type, which is what makes adding a job kind a matter of implementing IJob and calling TryAdd.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/IJob.cs#L3-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3e0705b11dd2d4b2cd02999a7c8448d5c30042f85f90a3cb74d0ccf759285ec3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L53-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0296a3afe80eed9634076b51c9fc26a623b8dd4be7ef3e5e484d002f409f9a42:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6c8ac59bd96147fabc4679990ed04eea",
      "statement": "ImplementSpec is the only production IJob and defines its Key as \"{owner}/{repository}#{issueNumber}\", so deduplication is scoped per GitHub issue: a repeated label, edit, or reopened delivery for an issue whose job is still running cannot start a second run.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L16-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a955c1a404b4715afb46ca47f8d16922c87579032e0878eaa869a362c6a56c5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1ecac1999f7e48318ba37a1541abd243",
      "statement": "TryAdd's dedupe contract is: insert job.Key into a ConcurrentDictionary<string, byte> keyed with StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase before attempting the channel write (so concurrent callers race on the dictionary and exactly one wins); if the channel write fails the key is removed again; and return false for a duplicate key without throwing or logging.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L17-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:05f91256084c327223ee2df4632256231126e26d53a5b9f53a0fb9408addf56b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1a0a3a73897f4624bf7584ac0a44f412",
      "statement": "The queue's reject path is deliberately not an error: GitHubWebhookProcessor calls TryAdd and, on false, emits only a Debug line (\"Implementation already running for {Repository}#{Number}\") while still returning a normal webhook response, so callers must not treat TryAdd == false as a failure or close/comment on the issue; the queue's only log statement of its own is LogFailed at Error level.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L81-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:49bb67e77a7e4f7d5399141e31623eb8db5f3d34370e07ae31d9fbbbc89a4537:"
        },
        {
