          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fcdac0c70d9309b2cfcf8695381dbc9fb449ecc75ac5d4212e5525cc38f911a7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_84ed98094ac94469a502e434299650dc",
      "statement": "The channel is Channel.CreateUnbounded<IJob>() with default options, so there is no backpressure and no queue depth to observe: TryAdd never blocks and returns false only for an in-flight key or an already-completed writer, a burst of events is buffered in process memory without any bound, and the ordering is FIFO with no prioritization.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L16-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5d4b758e2eda65fd15c59077d952ca16f8e89dc217b818cc9bd18ce506e65440:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L19-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ba0f76edd864f71ce38a2db8b2159144715200e8ede38475b8bafb3c23ea67f7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7f5a442cfd2a4c46aa84c5e188806ec4",
      "statement": "Failure isolation is a three-layer structure inside ExecuteAsync: a broad per-job catch that calls LogFailed(Exception, string) at Error level with template \"Job {Key} failed\"; a per-job catch (OperationCanceledException) when (stoppingToken.IsCancellationRequested) that swallows shutdown races but lets a genuine cancellation fall into the error path; and the same filtered catch around the loop itself; the broad catch is sanctioned by [SuppressMessage(\"Design\", \"CA1031\", Justification = \"A failed job must not tear down the queue.\")].",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L41-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f45a34a34cae6e11b500273221d2bac01f0738d8f1bd4eb8647c496e2203c122:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ed2b02b4ea4a4013a641a2ab635e6be7",
      "statement": "StopAsync completes the channel writer first and then calls base.StopAsync, which closes admission immediately (a post-shutdown TryAdd rolls its key back and returns false) but does not drain: cancellation of the internal stopping token ends ReadAllAsync and cancels the token handed to running jobs, so buffered jobs are abandoned unstarted and in-flight jobs observe cooperative cancellation that the shutdown filters do not log as failures.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L35-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:59644f0274d12cecd5ddf024e3ed1abd5b2e408edbf90b2d3892f0d4b4af5e7c:"
        },
        {
