          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7df83b338d016fa5e2819d3443695ebb54fe9e73e0a39f74363fa5b329b98b23:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7faf5dac6ad64bde8c9dc98762ed9db5",
      "statement": "JobQueueTests constructs the queue directly with a ServiceProvider over an empty ServiceCollection and a NullLogger and pins three behaviors: RunsAtMostTenJobsConcurrently asserts exactly 10 of 12 gated jobs start before release and all 12 eventually complete; ContinuesAfterJobFailure awaits both a throwing job's and a following job's completion; RejectsDuplicateKeyWhileJobRuns asserts TryAdd is false for the same key mid-run and true again afterwards via SpinWait.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/Sebastian.Tests/Jobs/JobQueueTests.cs#L9-L90",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0164f202390e5bb5468831d72581d60c8da3dd18f50d4e418871730c4b4e7734:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_89c9420bc1214b12b70d0c11f8e2e32d",
      "statement": "The queue's shutdown semantics are untested: no test asserts that TryAdd returns false after StopAsync, that a buffered job is abandoned rather than executed, that the OperationCanceledException filters behave as intended, or that a cancelled job is not logged as a failure, so the admission and failure-isolation paths are covered while the StopAsync/cancellation path is not.",
